= Prethesis and Thesis
Prethesis, thesis, and internship projects

I supervise *prethesis*, *thesis*, and *internship* projects at the School of Computer Science
and Engineering, International University (VNU-HCM). This page explains what that involves and
how to get in touch.

== The three kinds of project

~~~
{What I supervise}
- *Prethesis*: a first research project, usually in the final year of the undergraduate
  programme.
- *Thesis*: a full undergraduate or Master thesis, over one or two semesters.
- *Internship*: a shorter project, typically running for 8--16 weeks.

The label changes, the work does not: read the literature, choose one clear question, build or
reproduce a method, and measure it honestly.
~~~

== Co-supervision

Some of these projects are run jointly with a colleague, in which case there are two supervisors
and the scope is agreed between the three of us. Mention it in your message if you would like to
be considered for one of those.

~~~
{Co-advisor}
- *Name*: YOUR-CO-ADVISOR-NAME \M *Group*: YOUR-CO-ADVISOR-GROUP

Replace this box with the co-advisor's details, add one line per person if there is more than
one, or delete this whole section if every project is supervised on its own.
~~~

== What I work on

My current interests are distributed and federated learning, deep reinforcement learning for
networks, semantic communication, and wireless and mobile networking with the Internet of
Things. See [interests.html Research Interests] for the longer list and
[publications.html Publications] for the papers behind it.

The easiest way to find a topic is to open the two or three most recent papers on the
Publications page and ask which one you would like to understand deeply enough to extend.

== How we work

- One individual meeting each week, plus a group seminar.
- You are expected to read actively, write down what you understand, and present your work
  regularly -- including the weeks when it is not going well.
- The goal is a result you can defend: a clear question, a method, and evidence.

== How to get in touch

Write to [vtlphuong@hcmiu.edu.vn] and include:

- your *transcript* and your *CV*;
- a short statement of the topics you would like to work on;
- anything that shows how you work -- a course project, a report, a repository.

Say which of the three kinds of project you are applying for, and when you would start.

